00:30:03.280 --> 00:30:04.537
on our radar for events.

00:30:04.537 --> 00:30:06.370
FRANCESC CAMPOY: So I
have one more question

00:30:06.370 --> 00:30:08.703
that I need to ask before we
finish the interview, which

00:30:08.703 --> 00:30:11.714
is why is the company
called Improbable?

00:30:11.714 --> 00:30:13.630
ROB WHITEHEAD: Oh, that's
a really good story.

00:30:13.630 --> 00:30:16.690
I don't know-- let's see
where you can go with this.

00:30:16.690 --> 00:30:20.350
So actually, if you look at
our legal incorporation status,

00:30:20.350 --> 00:30:23.230
the name is Improbable Worlds.

00:30:23.230 --> 00:30:27.124
And I remember we hired a
very, very edgy design agency,

00:30:27.124 --> 00:30:28.540
and they were
hanging out with us.

00:30:28.540 --> 00:30:30.050
And I remember the last
thing they said to us--

00:30:30.050 --> 00:30:31.690
they were like,
"Drop the 'worlds.' "

00:30:31.690 --> 00:30:34.890
And then walked out in a kind
of quite enigmatic fashion.

00:30:34.890 --> 00:30:39.250
So yeah, I guess the
other side is it really

00:30:39.250 --> 00:30:40.930
has come to reflect
a lot of the values

00:30:40.930 --> 00:30:43.914
we have as a company,
really about trying

00:30:43.914 --> 00:30:46.080
to do things that haven't
been done before and felt,

00:30:46.080 --> 00:30:48.100
and specifically, these
large-scale simulations.

00:30:48.100 --> 00:30:49.183
So it's something we like.

00:30:49.183 --> 00:30:51.740
It's something which
definitely caught on.

00:30:51.740 --> 00:30:52.615
MARK MANDEL: Awesome.

00:30:52.615 --> 00:30:54.627
Well, Rob, thank you
